  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, single profile, PCA n2000) achieved 48.5% accuracy, while config_010 (image-only, ResNet50) was very weak at 20.8%, establishing RNA as the dominant modality. With only 2 data points, the key uncertainty is whether the RNA representation itself can be improved. Question: Does a learned non-linear RNA encoder (SCVI n200) outperform linear PCA (n2000) under the same single-profile setting? This is a clean single-variable comparison to config_001, isolating the effect of the RNA encoder. Why this experiment: If SCVI improves over PCA, it opens a promising branch (scvi + multiprofile, scvi + multimodal) for the remaining 7 experiments. If it does not, we avoid wasting budget on scvi-based configurations and can focus on multiprofile or a stronger image encoder. This is the highest-information, lowest-risk next step before committing to more complex multimodal or multiprofile designs."
}

